https://www.repairerdrivennews.com/2025/06/16/dirty-jobs-host-mike-rowe-talks-about-skilled-trade-shortage-during-dinner-in-detriot/

## Jim Farley

In November 2025 Ford CEO Jim Farley said Ford dealerships had about 5,000 open mechanic jobs and described the work as a $120,000/year job that takes roughly five years to learn.

That claim is unusually useful because it can be audited against:

- BLS wage distributions;
- the Department of Labor's description of flat-rate technician compensation;
- Ford's own technician-training paths;
- Ford's own recruiting language;
- current dealer job advertisements;
- technician-owned tool requirements;
- injury/working-condition data;
- technician retention and exit evidence;
- practitioner accounts made before and after Farley's statement.

